                    "rules": [
                        {
                            "id": "java-stored-command-injection",
                            "defaultConfiguration": {
                                "parameters": {
                                    "properties": {
                                        "CWE": "78",
                                        "owasp_top_10_2021": "A03",
                                        "owasp_top_10_llm": "LLM-02"
                                    }
                                }
                            },
                            "fullDescription": {
                                "text": "### Overview\nCommand Injection is a type of vulnerability that allows an attacker to\nexecute arbitrary code on a remote computer or device. This can allow the\nattacker to gain full control of the target system, potentially leading to\nsensitive information being compromised or unauthorized actions being performed.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\npublic class CommandiVulnerableServlet extends HttpServlet {\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String query = \"SELECT ip_address FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'\";\n        statement = connection.createStatement();\n        String ip = statement.executeQuery(query);\n        String cmd = \"ping -c 1 \" + ip;\n        Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this example, the `exec` command can be altered by a stored parameter that\nmight have been saved by an attacker, to execute arbitrary commands that can\nhack into the system.\n\n### Remediation\n```diff\npublic class CommandiSafeServlet extends HttpServlet {\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String query = \"SELECT ip_address FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'\";\n        statement = connection.createStatement();\n        String ip = statement.executeQuery(query);\n-         String cmd = \"ping -c 1 \" + ip;\n-         Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n+         String[] cmdArray = {\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", ip};\n+         Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmdArray);\n    }\n}\n```\nSplitting the stored data into the command and its parameters\nmakes the `exec` command safe.\n",
                                "markdown": "### Overview\nCommand Injection is a type of vulnerability that allows an attacker to\nexecute arbitrary code on a remote computer or device. This can allow the\nattacker to gain full control of the target system, potentially leading to\nsensitive information being compromised or unauthorized actions being performed.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\npublic class CommandiVulnerableServlet extends HttpServlet {\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String query = \"SELECT ip_address FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'\";\n        statement = connection.createStatement();\n        String ip = statement.executeQuery(query);\n        String cmd = \"ping -c 1 \" + ip;\n        Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this example, the `exec` command can be altered by a stored parameter that\nmight have been saved by an attacker, to execute arbitrary commands that can\nhack into the system.\n\n### Remediation\n```diff\npublic class CommandiSafeServlet extends HttpServlet {\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String query = \"SELECT ip_address FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'\";\n        statement = connection.createStatement();\n        String ip = statement.executeQuery(query);\n-         String cmd = \"ping -c 1 \" + ip;\n-         Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n+         String[] cmdArray = {\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", ip};\n+         Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmdArray);\n    }\n}\n```\nSplitting the stored data into the command and its parameters\nmakes the `exec` command safe.\n"
                            },
                            "help": {
                                "text": "### Overview\nCommand Injection is a type of vulnerability that allows an attacker to\nexecute arbitrary code on a remote computer or device. This can allow the\nattacker to gain full control of the target system, potentially leading to\nsensitive information being compromised or unauthorized actions being performed.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\npublic class CommandiVulnerableServlet extends HttpServlet {\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String query = \"SELECT ip_address FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'\";\n        statement = connection.createStatement();\n        String ip = statement.executeQuery(query);\n        String cmd = \"ping -c 1 \" + ip;\n        Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this example, the `exec` command can be altered by a stored parameter that\nmight have been saved by an attacker, to execute arbitrary commands that can\nhack into the system.\n\n### Remediation\n```diff\npublic class CommandiSafeServlet extends HttpServlet {\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String query = \"SELECT ip_address FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'\";\n        statement = connection.createStatement();\n        String ip = statement.executeQuery(query);\n-         String cmd = \"ping -c 1 \" + ip;\n-         Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);\n+         String[] cmdArray = {\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", ip};\n+         Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmdArray);\n    }\n}\n```\nSplitting the stored data into the command and its parameters\nmakes the `exec` command safe.\n"
                            },
                            "shortDescription": {
                                "text": "Stored Command Injection"
                            }
                        }
                    ],
